./.engramdb/memories/monthly-export-who-consumes-it-and-what-it-must_01a1082f-68da-77b2-90fa-1bc2617eb4b0.md:15:scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format requirements of the Finance import tool (it runs with a German locale and rejects anything else): the delimiter must be a semicolon (`;`), not a comma, and dates must be written `DD.MM.YYYY` (strftime `%d.%m.%Y`). UTF-8 without a BOM.
